  <text xml:lang="grc"><body xml:base="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0011.tyro.dindorf1893-grc1"><div type="edition" n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0011.tyro.dindorf1893-grc1" xml:lang="grc" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro"><head>ΤΥΡΩ Α. Β.</head><div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="573" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-573" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro">
            <note type="source">Aristoteles de Rhetorica II, 25.</note>
            <note type="commentary">Ἄλλος τόπος, τὸ ἀπὸ τοῦ ὀνόματος κατηγορεῖν, οἷον ὡς ὁ Σοφοκλῆς</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Σαφῶς Σιδηρὼ καὶ φοροῦσα τοὔνομα.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">Sidero Tyronis noverca.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="574" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-574" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro">
            <note type="source">Aristophanes Lysistrata v. 138.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Οὐκ ἐτὸς ἀφ᾽ ἡμῶν εἰσιν αἱ τραγωδίαι.</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">οὐδὲν γάρ ἐσμεν πλὴν Ποσειδῶν καὶ σκάφη.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">ubi scholiasta, Εἰς τὴν Σοφοκλέους δὲ Τυρὼ ταῦτα συντείνει ἐκθεῖσαν τὰ τέκνα εἰς σκάφην· Alius: Εἰς τὴν Τυρὼ δὲ Σοφοκλέους αἰνίττεται καθεῖσαν τὰ τέκνα εἰς σκάφος ὁ γὰρ Ποσειδῶν ἐμίγη Τυροῖ, καὶ ἐγέννησε Νηλέα καὶ Πελίαν.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="575" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-575" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro">
            <note type="source">Scholiasta Euripidis ad Orestem in fine :</note>
            <note type="commentary">Ἡ κατάληξις τῆς τραγῳδίας ἢ εἰς θρῆνον, ἢ εἰς πάθη καταλήγει· ἡ δὲ κωμῳδία γέλωτι καὶ εὐφροσύναις ἐνύφανται. ὅθεν ὁρᾶται τόδε τὸ δράμα κωμικῇ καταλήξει χρησάμενον. διαλλαγαὶ γὰρ πρὸς Μενέλαον καὶ Ὀρέστην. ἀλλὰ καὶ ἐν τῇ Ἀλκήστιδι ἐκ συμφορῶν εἰς εὐφροσύνην, καὶ ἐν Τυροῖ Σοφοκλέους ἀναγνώρισμα κατὰ τὸ τέλος γίνεται. (κατὰ τὸ ἀναγνώρισμα γέλως γ. Tyrwhitt ad Aristot. Poet. XXVI.)</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="576" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-576" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro">
            <note type="source">Aristoteles de Poetica cap. XVI.</note>
            <note type="commentary">Εἴδη δὲ ἀναγνωρίσεως. πρώτη μὲν ἡ διὰ σημείων. τούτων δὲ τὰ μὲν σύμφυτα, τὰ δὲ ἐπίκτητα· καὶ τούτων τὰ μὲν ἐν τῷ σώματι, οἷον οὐλαί· τὰ δὲ ἐκτὸς, τὰ περιδέραια. καὶ οἷον ἐν τῇ Τυροῖ διὰ τῆς σκάφης.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="577" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-577" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro">
            <note type="source">Pollux IV, 141.</note>
            <note type="commentary">ubi describit tragicas personas, Τυρὼ πελιδνὴ τὰς παρειάς παρὰ Σοφοκλεί.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="578" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-578" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0011.tyro.pearson1917-grc1:654">
            <note type="source">Scholiasta Aristophanis Avium v. 276</note>
            <note type="commentary">Ἔξεδρον χώραν ἔχων: ἐκ τῆς Σοφοκλέους δευτέρας Τυροῦς ἀρχὴ</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Τίς ὄρνις οὗτος ἔξεδρον χώραν ἔχων ;</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="579" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-579" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0011.tyro.nauck1889grc1:605">
            <note type="source">Athenæus III. p. 99 f.</note>
            <note type="commentary">Σοφοκλῆς τε ἐν Τυροῖ</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Σίτοισι παγχόρτοισιν ἐξενίζομεν.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="580" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-580" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0011.tyro.nauck1889grc1:599">
            <note type="source">Athenæus XI. p. 475 a.</note>
            <note type="commentary">Μνημονεύει δὲ τῶν καρχησίων καὶ Σοφοκλῆς Τυροῖ</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Προστῆναι μέσην</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">τράπεζαν ἀμφὶ σῖτα καὶ καρχήσια.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">πρὸς τὴν τράπεζαν φάσκων προσεληλυθέναι τοὺς δράκοντας, καὶ γενέσθαι περὶ τὰ σιτία καὶ τὰ καρχήσια. Proferuntur hæc etiam a Macrobio Saturn. V, 21.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="581" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-581" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0011.tyro.nauck1889grc1:600">
            <note type="source">Stobæus XX, 29.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Πόλλ᾽ ἐν κακοῖσι θυμὸς εὐνηθεὶς ὁρᾷ.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="582" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-582" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0011.tyro.nauck1889grc1:604">
            <note type="source">Stobæus XLVI, 6.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Ἄκων δ᾽ ἁμαρτὼν οὔ τις ἀνθρώπων κακός.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="583" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-583" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0011.tyro.nauck1889grc1:606">
            <note type="source">Stobæus LXXXVII, 3.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Πολλῶν δ᾽ ἐν πολυπληθίᾳ πέλεται,</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">οὔτ᾽ ἀπ᾿ εὐγενέων ἐσθλὸς οὔτ᾽ ἀχρείων</l>
              <l n="3" xml:lang="grc">τὸ λίαν κακός· βροτῷ δὲ πιστὸν οὐδέν.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="584" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-584" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0011.tyro.nauck1889grc1:602">
            <note type="source">Stobæus XCIX, 99.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Τίκτουσι γάρ τοι καὶ νόσους δυσθυμίαι.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="585" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-585" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0011.tyro.nauck1889grc1:592">
            <note type="source">Stobæus CIX, 2. Σοφοκλέους Τυροῦς β΄.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Μὴ σπεῖρε πολλοῖς τὸν παρόντα δαίμονα</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">σιγώμενος γάρ ἐστι θρηνεῖσθαι πρέπων.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="586" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-586" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0011.tyro.nauck1889grc1:603">
            <note type="source">Stobæus CXV, 8.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Γῆρας διδάσκει πάντα καὶ χρόνου τριβή.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="587" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-587" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro">
            <note type="source">Ælianus de N. A. II, 10.</note>
            <note type="commentary">Μάλιστα δὲ κομῶσα ἵππος ἁβροτάτη τέ ἐστι καὶ θρυπτικωτάτη. ἀτιμάζει γοῦν ἀναβῆναι τοὺς ὄνους αὐτὴν, ἵππῳ δὲ γαμουμένη ἥδεται, καὶ ἑαυτὴν ἀξιοῖ τῶν μεγίστων. ὅπερ οὖν συνειδότες οἱ βουλόμενοι ἡμιόνους σφίσι γενέσθαι, ἀποθρίσαντες τῆς ἵππου τὴν χαίτην εἰκῆ καὶ ὡς ἔτυχεν, εἶτα μέντοι τοὺς ὄνους ἐπάγουσιν· ἡ δὲ ὑπομένει τὸν ἄδοξον ἤδη γαμέτην, πρῶτον αἰδουμένη. καὶ Σοφοκλῆς δὲ ἔοικε μεμνῆσθαι τοῦ πάθους. (Conf. Plutarch. Moral. p. 754 a.) Morem equas tondendi, quo facilius asinos admittant, tan it rursus XII, 16. versusque</note>
          </div>
        <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="588" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-588" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro">
            <note type="source">Antiatticista p. 89, 19.</note>
            <quote>Δυσθυμία: Σ. Τυροί.</quote>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="589" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-589" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0011.tyro.nauck1889grc1:594">
            <note type="source">Photius p. 17, 7.</note>
            <quote>Ἐρρηνοβοσκός: ὁ προβατοβοσκὸς ἐν Τυροῖ β΄ Σοφοκλέους. ἴσως ἀπὸ τοῦ ἄρην.</quote>
            <note type="commentary">Conf. Etymolog. M. p. 377, 22. et Hesychium in ἀρηνοβοσκός.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="590_591" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-590_591" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0011.tyro.nauck1889grc1:591">
            <note type="source">Hesychius.</note>
            <quote>Ἔχθιμα: μισήματα. Σ. Τυροῖ.</quote>
            <note type="commentary">Codex τυράννοις, correctum ab Piersono ad Mæridem p. 436. Idem Hesychius, Καρπομανής: εἰς κόρον ἐξυβρίζουσα. Σοφοκλῆς τυριλάω. Fortasse Τυροῖ β (δευτέρᾳ) vel α.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="592" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-592" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0011.tyro.nauck1889grc1:608">
            <note type="source">Antiatticista p. 98, 11.</note>
            <quote>Ἤνεγκον: ἐπὶ πρώτου προσώπου. Σ. Τυροῖ.</quote>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="593" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-593" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0011.tyro.pearson1917-grc1:650">
            <note type="source">Hesychius.</note>
            <quote>Θεανὴ νῆσος: ἡ ἐκ θεοῦ θεία. Σ. Τυροῖ ά.</quote>
            <note type="commentary">Scrib. Θεία νόσος· ἡ ἐκ θεοῦ.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="594" xml:id="fragment-tyro-dindorf1893_grc1-594" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0011_tyro">
            <note type="source">Etymolog. M. p. 747, 49.</note>
            <quote>Ταυροφάγον: τὸν Διόνυσον. Σοφοκλῆς ἐν Τυροῖ. ὅτι τοῖς τὸν διθύραμβον νικήσασι βοῦς ἐδίδοτο. ἢ τὸν ὠμηστήν.</quote>
            <note type="commentary">Conf. schol. Aristoph. Ranar. v. 360. Photium p. 571, 13. et Suidam in Ταυροφάγον.</note>
          </div>
        </div></body></text></TEI>
